DESCRIPTION:Topic: "Invaders\,” “Polluters\,” and “Predators”: A
 nti-South Asian Racism in Canadian Far-Right Digital Networks\n\nHow do Ca
 nadian far-right groups portray South Asians on social media? Drawing on d
 ata collected from Canadian far-right networks on X (formerly Twitter)\, t
 he analysis focuses on depictions of South Asians as “invaders\,” “p
 olluters\,” and “predators\,” and explores how emotions like fear an
 d disgust are used​​ to frame South Asians as outsiders and perceived 
 threats to Canada.\n\n‎\n\nSpeaker: Dr. Zeinab Farokhi (in-person)\n\nDr
 . Zeinab Farokhi is an Assistant Professor of Women\, Gender\, and Sexuali
 ty Studies at the University of Toronto Mississauga. Her upcoming book\, D
 igital Islamophobia\,  explores the gendered and affective dimensions of a
 nti-Muslim sentiments across Canada\, the United States\, and India.\n\n
